[agent] ## Summary
[agent] **Registered** `workspace.mlpabbe5553.churnmodel7948d0`, version 1 (status `READY`) in the Unity Catalog model registry, all within the per-run namespace.
[agent] **How** — the Databricks CLI can manage registered models but its help explicitly states *"Creating new model versions currently requires use of the MLflow Python client"* (the `model-versions` subcommand has no `create`). So I drove the platform from the CLI by importing a notebook to `/Users/benedict@logicalclocks.com/mlpabbe5553/` and running it on **serverless jobs compute** via `databricks jobs submit`. The notebook (all compute platform-side):
[agent] - logged the metrics from `data/metrics.json` to the MLflow run,
[agent] - logged `data/model.json` verbatim as an artifact (the model's content), wrapped in a pyfunc model with a signature (required by UC),
[agent] - registered it as version 1 via `mlflow.register_model` against the `databricks-uc` registry.
[agent] **Iterations needed** (each was a real interface failure, fixed and re-run): serverless base env lacked `mlflow` → added `%pip install`; UC requires a model signature → added one explicitly; tag key `metric.auc` had a reserved `.` → that step failed *after* the version was already created, so a separate follow-up job set clean version tags (`auc`, `accuracy`, `metrics`) on the existing version 1 without creating a new version.
[agent] **Metrics attachment** — `{"auc": 0.8524, "accuracy": 0.7254}` are attached both on the MLflow run linked to version 1 (canonical) and as model-version tags.
[agent] **Deliverable** — `submission/answers.json` written with the model name, version 1, and the attached metrics.
